*Heading
OP=NEW that removes a support: a propped B31 cantilever and an S4 plate
** Cantilever L = 1000, RECT 20 (z, local 1) x 40 (y), E = 210000, z tip load P = 10: propped
** at mid-span (step 1) the tip deflects 7 P L^3 / (96 E I) = 0.1302, free (step 2) P L^3 /
** (3 E I) = 0.5952, with I = 40 * 20^3 / 12.  The S4 plate (1000 x 200 x 10, beside it) is
** clamped along x = 0 and tip-loaded in both steps, so its tip deflection must not change.
** Step 2 removes the prop with OP=NEW and repeats the clamps.  ccx 2.23 does not rebuild
** re-specified rotational BCs on shell/beam nodes after OP=NEW (the beam root turns into a
** hinge, the plate root too), so abq2ccx makes those nodes knots (knot beams), whose BCs
** OP=NEW handles; a knot holds the beam section rigid (~0.7 % stiffer clamp).
